  pages:
  - text: "I took the gravekeeper\u2019s job because no one else would. Not after
      the last man left without a word, abandoning his post. The cemetery sat on
      the edge of town. People whispered that he fled in the middle of the night,
      though no one could agree on what finally scared him off. All they knew was
      that they needed someone new for the job."
    font: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
    fontSize: 48
    textColor: {r: 0.9811321, g: 0.9811321, b: 0.9811321, a: 1}
    image: {fileID: 0}
    minimumDisplayTime: 0
  - text: "Folks kept coming to me, asking if I could keep an eye on what they\u2019d
      buried. This town had a strange fixation on laying people to rest with their
      belongings, and lately outsiders had started digging them back up. Gangs were
      moving closer, and the cemetery was an easy target. So now I walk the rows
      with a flashlight, not because I feel brave, but because I need the pay and
      no one else will do it."
    font: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
    fontSize: 48
    textColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    image: {fileID: 0}
    minimumDisplayTime: 0
  - text: 
    font: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
    fontSize: 48
    textColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8a56a59210eece140b280ab8339dcf39, type: 3}
    minimumDisplayTime: 2
